## My QR Passes consolidation (commit `c2b3c5e`)

Mirrors the iOS `CheckInQRView`: the participant "My QR Passes" hub now shows
the arrival check-in QR codes **and** the provided-bus boarding tickets (with
the Stripe fare CTA) — a passenger no longer needs a separate Transportation
screen. `CheckInQrPassesRoute` loads bookings via `TransportationViewModel` and
the user's lodging via `MyLodgingViewModel`; the passenger "Transportation"
entry was removed from the camp-detail resources. (The standalone
`TransportationTicketsRoute` remains registered but is no longer linked from the
detail resources — safe to retire later.)

## D3 Lodging

- **Model**: the `LodgingUnit` model + `LodgingKind`/`LodgingGenderPolicy` enums
  + `LodgingPayload`/`toLodgingUnitOrNull` already existed (A10 data-model pass).
  Extended in place: added `LodgingGenderPolicy.accepts(gender)` and
  `LodgingUnit.occupancy`/`availableSpots`/`occupancyText`/`contains`. Did NOT
  duplicate the model.
- **Service** (`data/lodging/LodgingService.kt`): interface + Firestore (snapshot
  listener, `LodgingPayload` write, create-only `createdAt`, `setOccupants` merge)
  + reactive `FakeLodgingService` + Hilt binding. Collection
  `campings/{id}/lodging/{unitId}`.
- **Admin** (`ui/lodging/`): `LodgingViewModel` (gated `canManageTeams`,
  `Restricted` otherwise) + `LodgingScreen` (summary, gender-policy filter chips,
  unit cards with occupant rows, "Needs a bed" section) + editor & assignment
  `ModalBottomSheet`s. Camp-detail "Lodging" entry gated `canManageTeams`.
- **Participant**: `MyLodgingCard` + `MyLodgingViewModel` (read-only observe)
  embedded in My QR Passes — self-silences when there's no lodging.
- **i18n**: lodging strings added to EN, PT-BR, FR.

## Data contract

- Wire keys `campingID` / `occupantIDs` (iOS casing); `kind` ∈
  tent/cabin/room/dorm; `genderPolicy` ∈ any/male/female/family; capacity int
  clamped ≥ 1; `createdAt` first-create only, `updatedAt` every write
  (serverTimestamp). Occupancy denormalized into `occupantIDs[]` (no assignment
  collection).

## Deferred (iOS extra, not in the Android contract)

- One-tap auto-allocation (capacity + gender + family rules). Hand assignment +
  the gender/capacity eligibility checks are in place; the allocator itself is
  not ported.
